Use Windows.pkg
/* THE ABOUT TEXT, bound as res_AboutFile - the DFAbout library's name, which its DfAbout.pkg reads as it compiles:
   it binds ..\Help\About.rtf under that name unless UseCustomAboutResource says the program does, so the define and
   the binding come BEFORE the Use that brings DfAbout.pkg in (error 4328 otherwise). This program's About text is
   Help\AboutFT.html, beside the classic program's About.rtf - bound here, where FTStdAbout.pkg would bind
   Help\About.html otherwise; it is a resource, so a change to it takes a rebuild. The library's About dialog shows
   it after the facts because a file was bound (pbShowAboutFile of the dialog is True then). */
Define UseCustomAboutResource for 1
Include_Resource ..\Help\AboutFT.html as res_AboutFile type DF_RESOURCE_TYPE_BINARY
Use FTStdAbout.pkg               // RDCFlexTron: StdAbout.pkg's twin - Activate_About and DoAbout, the About dialog

/*  ABOUT (2026-10-08) - the library's About dialog (cFTAboutDialog, RDCFlexTron 0.9.18), shown the way the classic
    program shows the DFAbout library's: the client area Uses this file where it Used StdAbout.pkg, and its
    Activate_About sends DoAbout with the mark - the same line as DFRefactor.src's. The page: the mark, the name and
    the build facts the DFAbout library gathers, the About text above, and the Powered by DataFlex mark; System
    information, Copy and Close. This file held the page itself from 2026-10-06 to 2026-10-08 (as AboutFT.dg, with
    SystemInfoFT.dg and AppHtml\CssStyle\about.css); the library's ftabout.css draws it now. */
